    "verdict": "`net` = tr_M^{z=1} - h*(coefficient of the longest element), exactly, on all six basis elements. So the corpus's 'the counit and the Markov trace are genuinely distinct functionals' is sharpened to a single rank-one difference supported on w_0, and its companion 'they agree precisely when z=1' turns out to be a statement about Delta's SUPPORT (Delta has zero w_0 coordinate) rather than about the functionals -- on T_{w_0} they differ by h at every z. Two consequences: the ladder phase is a transport WITHIN one family, 2*alpha(z) = tr_M^1(Delta) - tr_M^z(Delta); and because tr_M^{z=1} annihilates [H,H], the entire z-free floor IS the rank-one term, net(dC) = -h*(dC)_{w_0} = -h*a_(2,1), exactly. Read with chi^(2,1)(Delta) = 0 from the block resolution: the 2-dimensional block contributes nothing to the trace-visible part of the phase and everything to the trace-invisible part. Its contribution was never absent -- it was in the sector no trace can see. Scope-(a): nothing derived about the correction, nothing wired."
